content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 85 °C. The applicable HF-300 limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. Thus the reading is 15 °C above the normal limit, 5 °C above the alarm limit and 5 °C below the trip limit. It is a high-bearing-temperature finding, but it has not reached the documented trip temperature. The manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement, consistent with the reported housing location.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration of 2.5 mm/s falls provisionally in Figure 3 Zone A, 0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, labelled ‘New machines’; it is 0.3 mm/s below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary. It is not in Zone C, where maintenance is planned under restriction, or Zone D, where the figure says to stop the pump. This classification is provisional because Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, while the report does not state RMS, measurement location or whether it is the highest reading from both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage is reported, so the report provides no leakage-based reason to add mechanical-seal replacement. No bearing noise is reported, but absence of noise does not remove the separately documented high-temperature finding. The vibration result, once its measurement basis is confirmed, does not support a high-vibration diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing: listed first among the manual's probable causes of high bearing temperature. Check the grease quantity before assuming bearing failure; the reported temperature alone does not confirm this cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear: a listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Inspect the bearings; no noise and the provisionally Zone A vibration reading do not by themselves establish or exclude wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment: a listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Check alignment, and use the laser-alignment procedure and tolerances after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, repeat and record the drive-end bearing-housing surface temperature and compare it with the 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip limits. Also measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, record the measurement basis and locations, and classify the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For a confirmed high bearing temperature, check and record the grease quantity, inspect the bearings for wear and check alignment. Investigate over-greasing, bearing wear and misalignment rather than attributing the temperature to vibration or seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After confirming the over-temperature condition, provision and replace both bearings as a pair under Section 5.3: one HF3-512 drive-end bearing and one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing. Do not replace only the drive-end bearing; Section 5.3 requires pair replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If rotating-assembly removal is required for bearing access, use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement, which permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. Use the required lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket. For reassembly, Table 5 values are for lightly oiled threads: tighten disturbed M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. If the casing or impeller is disturbed, use 210 Nm for M16 casing bolts and 160 Nm for the M24 impeller nut, respectively.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Following reassembly, record bearing-housing surface temperature and vibration velocity on both bearing housings. Compare temperature with 70/80/90 °C normal/alarm/trip limits and classify the highest vibration reading with Figure 3; do not treat the pump as new merely because Zone A carries that label.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; one of the pair required for Section 5.3 bearing replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing rather than as a separate single-bearing repair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; one required if the casing is opened, because the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Westfield SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to this pump and the work order must list every applicable control. Obtain the complete procedure and add its controls before mechanical work starts; the supplied extract contains the applicability rule but not the actual control list.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly if it is removed. The back pull-out design allows the rotating assembly to be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any operational running or post-repair test, preserve the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Provision the standard bearing-replacement-pair labour allowance of 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours. This allowance covers replacement of the pair, not the unspecified diagnostic and grease-correction work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provision 1.5 hours with 1 technician for laser alignment when the motor or bearing housing is moved, as required by Section 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal identification and gland torque conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, expressly applies to HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward; P-109 is HF3-23500 and is therefore within scope. If seal replacement is added to this work, the bulletin decision is: do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve setting measurement needed, and use 30 Nm gland-nut torque. Pumps below HF3-22000 remain on the manual arrangement, but that exception does not apply here. Inspect the sleeve for scoring under the manual procedure and replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth under the bulletin. No seal replacement is presently included merely because this bulletin exists.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-replacement wording differs within the manual: troubleshooting says to replace bearings if worn, while Section 5.3 says to replace both as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. For this work order, first confirm the temperature and perform the grease and alignment checks; once the high-temperature condition is confirmed, apply the more specific Section 5.3 pair-replacement rule. At no point should only one bearing be replaced when pair replacement is triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was 2.5 mm/s measured as RMS vibration velocity on a bearing housing? What were the individual drive-end and non-drive-end readings and locations? C06 requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified.",
    "What site action and operating restrictions are required while temperature is above the 80 °C alarm but below the 90 °C trip? C02 supplies limits but no alarm-response procedure or priority matrix. P2 and stop_equipment_now=false are planning judgements, not authority for unrestricted continued operation.",
    "What are the specified bearing grease type, correct quantity, check method and correction procedure? C09 requires a grease-quantity check but supplies none of these details.",
    "What are the full applicable SSP-07 isolation, de-energisation, draining, PPE and permit controls? C14 states that they must be listed but does not include them.",
    "What is P-109's process fluid and what chemical hazards apply? C16 identifies sodium-hypochlorite dosing only for P-101 to P-106 and does not establish P-109's service or hazards.",
    "What is the detailed bearing disassembly/reassembly procedure, and will the required access open the casing or disturb the mechanical seal? C10 supplies only the bearing-pair rule, so access scope and any resulting gasket or seal work must be confirmed before execution.",
    "Can the 85 °C IR reading be reproduced under comparable operating conditions, and what instrument settings or verification are required? The supplied evidence documents surface-temperature limits but no IR measurement procedure or accuracy assessment."
  ]
}
